SC2SLR: add the paper's two-view NT-Xent contrastive loss

Why: the paper's method (Sec. 3.3, Eq. 3, Eq. 8, Fig. 2) trains with
L = L_CTC^F + L_CTC^S + L_KL + L_NT-Xent over two augmented views, but the
released code has no second view, no NT-Xent, and no contrastive term;
its loss is ConvCTC + SeqCTC + Dist only. The released dataloader does carry
an unused deep_transform() with SimCLR's color jitter (0.4,0.4,0.4,0.1, p 0.8),
grayscale (p 0.2) and Gaussian blur (sigma 0.1-2, p 0.5), the appearance
augmentations the paper lists, plus a commented-out deep_aug call; this patch
wires those in. utils/video_augmentation.py used transforms, F, Image and
ImageFilter without importing them, so deep_transform() could not run.

Design (documented guesses; the paper gives no temperature, projection head,
pooling, or weight sharing):
- each training clip gets the released spatial/temporal augmentation once,
  then two independent deep_transform() views; keypoint heatmap added to both;
- both views go through the same (weight-shared) network as one 2B batch,
  views of a sample adjacent so pack_padded_sequence keeps sorted lengths;
- every released loss (ConvCTC, SeqCTC, Dist with the released weights) is
  computed on both views; labels are repeated per view;
- NT-Xent, temperature 0.5 (SimCLR default), weight 1 (Eq. 8), on the BiLSTM
  sequential features mean-pooled over valid time steps, no projection head;
  negatives are the other 2(N-1) views in the batch (Sec. 3.3).
Evaluation is unchanged: dev/test clips are single-view.
Applies after sc2slr-1-keypoint-glue.patch.
